{
  "id": "Compound::DB00376 - Gene::1131",
  "verbalization": "Trihexyphenidyl, a muscarinic acetylcholine receptor antagonist, is shown to bind to Chrm5 and Chrm4, both of which are involved in G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity. This binding is further linked to the participation of these receptors in the broader process of Chrm3 activation. The evidence suggests that Trihexyphenidyl may influence Chrm3 through its interaction with muscarinic receptors, potentially modulating their activity. The shared involvement of Chrm3 in G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity across different receptor subtypes implies a common downstream pathway, possibly involving G-protein signaling. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Trihexyphenidyl could interact with Chrm3, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
